{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"423bd7682aff4eaa8b6551c66e676ebafd15a3895abb67a75801a7ec3098c878","slug":"research.pred-responses","location":"/research/pred_responses.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Predicting individualized brain responses","content_includes_title":false,"github":"https://github.com/feilonglab/feilonglab.github.io.git","copyright":"2025-2026, the Feilong Lab","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/feilonglab/feilonglab.github.io.git/blob/main/research/pred_responses.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/feilonglab/feilonglab.github.io.git/edit/main/research/pred_responses.md","thumbnail":"/topographic_idiosync-0b79e1f689e237e7382c40b14b86888b.png","thumbnailOptimized":"/topographic_idiosync-0b79e1f689e237e7382c40b14b86888b.webp","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"pred_responses.md","url":"/pred_responses-34d2fa2323a9fabeb9bf95ce4ac48e0c.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Topographic idiosyncrasies","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"prwJ4zINLf"}],"identifier":"topographic-idiosyncrasies","label":"Topographic idiosyncrasies","html_id":"topographic-idiosyncrasies","implicit":true,"key":"WhMOHos8IS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Different brains encode the same information in distinct ways ","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"aIdTwVQJEv"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","children":[{"type":"cite","kind":"parenthetical","label":"haxby2020","identifier":"haxby2020","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Haxby ","key":"E4ZcAhi1ME"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"et al.","key":"dgGSuXpRkZ"}],"key":"oizuwHklST"},{"type":"text","value":", 2020","key":"kXBahdj7Yv"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"Hqb56hBjnl"}],"key":"zZDcOAdmfk"},{"type":"text","value":".\nAcross individuals, the same brain function may be implemented in different anatomical locations, while the same anatomical region may support different functions.\nThese idiosyncrasies in the correspondence between function and anatomy---often referred to as topographic idiosyncrasies---pose a major challenge for studying brain function across individuals.","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"Y7x5e3ghMM"}],"key":"erTtsILrSv"},{"type":"card","children":[{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/topographic_idiosync-0b79e1f689e237e7382c40b14b86888b.png","align":"left","key":"Gb698dNhCS","urlSource":"topographic_idiosyncrasies.png","urlOptimized":"/topographic_idiosync-0b79e1f689e237e7382c40b14b86888b.webp"}],"label":"topographic_idiosyncrasies","identifier":"topographic_idiosyncrasies","enumerator":"1","html_id":"topographic-idiosyncrasies","key":"oCXhbBlTb4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fig 1. Topographic idiosyncrasies.","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"Kgdk3575tE"}],"key":"BsFUw3WWVe"},{"type":"text","value":"\nWithin each brain, response patterns to a given stimulus are reliable across independent measurements (top and bottom rows).\nThe brain shows distinct response patterns to different stimuli (left and middle columns).\nHowever, across brains, response patterns to the same stimulus differ (left and right columns).\nSee ","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"kU3RwNnOId"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"narrative","children":[{"type":"cite","kind":"narrative","label":"feilong2025","identifier":"feilong2025","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feilong & Zhang (2025)","key":"Cz6QUw4E3T"}],"enumerator":"2","key":"SDTbSgsDnx"}],"key":"sgl5B9ZVil"},{"type":"text","value":" for a discussion of how these idiosyncrasies can be resolved","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"MpMWRLzvQa"}],"key":"kpXBZ6fhxV"}],"key":"hbWUW7KItv"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Predicting individualized brain responses","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"CGt9Ryo5c9"}],"identifier":"predicting-individualized-brain-responses","label":"Predicting individualized brain responses","html_id":"predicting-individualized-brain-responses","implicit":true,"key":"spUFYRFzII"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To study these functional regions, rather than anatomical locations, researchers often use functional localizers to identify these regions in each individual brain.\nHowever, acquiring such data can be challenging in many studies.\n","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"CFwHdzw6KD"},{"type":"link","url":"/research/hyperalignment","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hyperalignment","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"MC6m9xgFFH"}],"urlSource":"hyperalignment.md","dataUrl":"/research.hyperalignment.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"by4yq85HvA"},{"type":"text","value":" ","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"jkjAFqmLxd"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","children":[{"type":"cite","kind":"parenthetical","label":"haxby2020","identifier":"haxby2020","children":[{"type":"text","value"